                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the brand impressions`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `The brand-tracker is on the table: <strong>warmth 72</strong>, <strong>competence 58</strong>, <strong>morality 49</strong> and falling, and stated purchase intent down from 62% to <strong>55%</strong>. No strategy is prescribed. Žabkar’s framework says sustainability moves <em>specific</em> impressions, not a generic halo. Identify which impression is the <em>binding constraint</em> on intent, which segment is most at risk, and how the chain from spend → impression → intent is actually breaking. Vista is warm but its integrity is under public attack — read the data before you spend a euro.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Plan: map investments to impressions`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Before committing the budget, map it. Decide <strong>which sustainability initiative</strong> to fund and <strong>which channel</strong> to deploy — and tag each to the impression it is meant to move. The discovery: third-party-audited claims and certification lift <em>morality and competence</em>; community and cause work lifts <em>warmth</em>; and <strong>communication without substance behind it reads as greenwashing and lowers morality further</strong>. Which euro is buying which perception?`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Decide: allocate the €14M and project intent`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `The core round. Commit the <strong>€14M</strong> across sustainability substance and communication. The constraint is real — you cannot fund everything, and <em>substance must precede or accompany the message</em> to avoid backfire. Heavy comms moves perception fastest but, ungrounded, invites a second greenwashing hit; substantive initiatives build durable morality but take time to register. Balance the morality deficit against the warmth and competence that sustain the premium — and sequence the proof before the amplification.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Recover: fact-check & defend to the board`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Two events land. A <strong>journalist fact-checks</strong> your new sustainability claim — if the substance is real, the morality gain survives; if not, it collapses. And <strong>Polje cuts price 8%</strong> to pressure your premium. Show the signals hold under scrutiny: morality survives verification, intent holds without matching the cut, and the premium is defended on perceived superiority — not discounting. Then make the board case to the CFO on a defensible <em>ROMI</em>, not reach.`,

