                    insight_signal:         `Brand signal mastered: you treated sustainability as differentiated signals, not a halo. Verified substance lifted morality and competence, grounded communication converted them into purchase intent above 60%, the premium held on perceived superiority, and the spend defends as a real ROMI. That is Žabkar’s chain — spend → impression → intent — run end to end.`,
                    insight_greenwash:      `Greenwashing backlash: communication outran the substance behind it, so amplification read as hypocrisy and morality fell further instead of recovering. The fact-check found a claim you could not back — exactly the failure the research warns about. Silence would have done less damage than an ungrounded campaign.`,
                    insight_wrongmuscle:    `Strengthened the strong muscle: you poured spend into warmth, which was already at 72, while morality — the dimension actually under attack and blocking intent — barely moved. You polished what was winning and left the binding constraint unaddressed.`,
                    insight_pricewar:       `Surrendered the premium: faced with Polje’s 8% cut you discounted instead of defending on perceived superiority. You told consumers Vista is not worth its price and gave away the margin that funds the brand — the premium is defended by impressions, not by matching cuts.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed campaign: some signals landed, but substance, communication and sequencing did not fully reinforce each other. Purchase intent and morality moved unevenly, leaving enough doubt for the board to question whether the premium and the ROMI are secure.`,
                    insight_morality_low:   `Morality never recovered: the dimension the watchdog attacked stayed weak, so even reach and warmth could not lift purchase intent. For a sustainability brand, morality is the conversion lever — and it was left short.`,
                    insight_intent_low:     `Purchase intent finished below the 60% target: the impressions did not move enough in the dimensions that convert, so finance’s 20% budget cut and the mid-tier repositioning are now on the table.`,
                    insight_romi_low:       `The ROMI is not defensible: you spent without tying the intent lift to incremental margin. The CFO judges return, not reach — and this allocation reads as a campaign, not an investment.`,
                    insight_nosubstance:    `You never funded verifiable substance: every signal you raised rested on claims you could not prove, leaving morality exposed to the next fact-check and the brand one accusation from another credibility hit.`,

                    hint_greenwash:         `You have triggered a greenwashing backlash — comms ran ahead of substance and morality is falling. Fund verifiable, third-party action and let the proof land before you amplify again.`,
                    hint_morality:          `Morality is the binding constraint and it is still under 52. Aim verified substance and a credibility-led channel at integrity — that is the dimension converting (or blocking) intent.`,
                    hint_wrongmuscle:       `You are feeding warmth, already your strongest dimension. Redirect spend to morality — the deficit the watchdog is exploiting — or intent will not move.`,
                    hint_premium:           `You have surrendered the 18% premium by discounting. Defend on perceived superiority — stronger morality and competence — not on price, before the margin erodes further.`,
                    hint_romi:              `Your ROMI is weak — you are spending faster than the intent lift justifies. Tie every euro to the impression and the incremental margin it produces before the board review.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — intent above target, morality recovered, premium intact. Land it: verify the claim under the fact-check and make the case to the CFO on ROMI, not reach.`,

